# Which creature Clone may copy is judged as it is now, but what it takes is only the copiable values (CR 707.2): an
# animated Mutavault is a creature and may be chosen, yet its animation is an effect, not a copiable value, so the Clone
# is a Mutavault that is a land and nothing else (the card's ruling on copying an animated manland). On turn 1 Bot1 taps
# Mutavault for {C} and spends it on Mutavault's own animation, then casts Clone with Black Lotus and Mox Sapphire,
# copying the 2/2 Mutavault, the lone creature. The Clone is a land with no creature type, not a creature (so not a 0/0
# that dies), and was not played as a land; the original is still a 2/2 Land Creature until end of turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mutavault
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Clone
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mutavault.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: {T})
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: {1})
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Clone.Cast
Bot1.Accept
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Mutavault; Mutavault; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#1.Types = Land; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#1.Subtypes = (every creature type)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#2.Types = Land
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#2.Subtypes = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault#2.Colors = (absent)
